From e59ccfffc4b5fcde94994810ef6a915262bafa81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:05:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp tr098] P4d: the X_AIS_IPv6 leaves of both WAN objects,
 46 parameters

wan_device_v6_* for the X_AIS_IPv6 subtree and wan_device_{get,set}_x_ais_ipv6_*
for the flat leaves, plus json_get_gw() and is_ipv6_public() of
functions/common/common.

New file this time, wanipv6_mtk.c: these 46 parameters share nothing with the
IPv4 leaves except the entry they hang off.  What they do share is the entry
model, so struct wan_entry and the enumeration move to wanconn_mtk.h and
wanip_mtk.c exports them -- eight helpers, four of which were renamed out of
the generic namespace they were in (sect_opt -> wan_sect_opt, entry_opt,
str_is_uint, iface_status likewise).  P4e and P4f will need the same header.

Two shapes, and they are not the same set.  The "X_AIS_IPv6." subtree is
identical on both objects: 13 leaves.  The flat "X_AIS_IPv6<Name>" leaves are
not -- WANIPConnection has 12 and spells the status one X_AIS_IPv6ConnStatus,
WANPPPConnection has 8 and spells it X_AIS_IPv6ConnectionStatus and has no
GatewayType / GatewayAddress / DNSType / PrefixDelegationType /
GUAFromPrefixEnable at all.  Kept exactly: an ACS template written against one
object must not find new parameters on the other.

Where the shapes overlap they are not aliases.  X_AIS_IPv6.AddressingType
reads v6_mode alone; X_AIS_IPv6AddressingType reads v6_active first and
answers "None" when IPv6 is off.  X_AIS_IPv6AutoModeEnable can only move the
entry between DHCP and Static, never back to SLAAC -- only the addressing-type
leaf can do that.

The guard rails are the part an ACS will hit, so they are verbatim: address,
prefix length, gateway and external address are refused (9001) unless v6_mode
is Static; Pd.Enable is refused when it IS Static; DNSServers is refused while
v6_static_dns is 0; ManualDNS cannot be turned off in Static mode (9007).

The two DNSServers leaves are deliberately not per entry: they read and write
the space separated list dhcp.lan.dns, so every instance shows the same pair.
That is what the product does and why they never joined the subtree.

wan_device_v6_get_ipaddr()'s fallback -- "ip -6 addr show dev <l3_device>"
when ubus reports no address -- reads /proc/net/if_inet6 here instead of
spawning a process, and inet_ntop()s the raw hex to the same compressed form.

One difference: X_AIS_IPv6ConnStatus is writable and the shell ran ifup /
ifdown inline, cutting the session it was answering on.  Queued for the end of
the session, the same as WANPPPConnection.Reset in the previous commit.

Data model: 301 -> 347 of 783.  verify-dm-paths phase 4 now 145/173 with 0
extras, and the 28 left are exactly PortMapping (P4e) and X_AIS_ServiceList
(P4f).  111 claims across 13 modules, 0 overlaps.

NOT BUILD-TESTED on this host: no compiler here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
